// Package mc holds motion-compensation kernels: H.264 quarter-sample luma
// interpolation (six-tap, put and average forms for every fractional
// position) and, later, eighth-sample chroma interpolation, the weighted and
// default combination of two predictions, and the HEVC and AV1 separable
// filters producing 16-bit intermediates.
//
// Implemented: PutLuma and AvgLuma (ITU-T H.264 clause 8.4.2.2.1 with the
// default averaging of clause 8.4.2.3.1), for the seven luma block sizes. On
// arm64 they run NEON kernels generated by internal/genmc (go generate); on
// every other target, and with the purego tag, they run the portable
// reference. Both are bit-exact with the standard.
//
// Also implemented: WeightUni and WeightBi, explicit weighted prediction
// (clause 8.4.2.3.2, Equations 8-274 to 8-276); WeightBi with equal weights
// 2^logWD is the default average and runs the fused AvgLuma kernel.
//
// See docs/design/design.md.
package mc
